                <pb facs="0538" n="430" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg430"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/718: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-03T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 3,
                                1927—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>396. Your 1044, November 29, 11 a.m. Department considers that tax referred to by
                    Consul General Shanghai is a violation of treaty when collected on American
                    goods re-exported from one open port to another or shipped to the interior under
                    transit pass. As regards question of protest see Department’s telegram No. 270,
                    July 1, 5 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
